<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n49466" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θύρ-αζε</span></b> 
		<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">[ῠ]</span>, Adv., for
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θύρασδε</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>to the door</i>, and so, <i>out of doors</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐκ δὲ θ. ἔδραμον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					18.29
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				416
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Od.
				15.62
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δόμων ἐξῆγε θ.</span> ib.<i><span class="en">
				465
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> generally,
				<i>out</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Il.
				5.694
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Od.
				15.451
			</span></i>, etc.; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἔκβασις . . ἁλὸς πολιοῖο
				θ.</span> a way of getting <i>out of</i> the sea, <i><span class="en">
				5.410
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἰχθὺν ἐκ πόντοιο θ.
			[ἕλκειν</span>] <i><span class="en">
				Il.
				16.408
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				21.237
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπὶ πρύμνῃσιν ἐείλεον οὐδὲ θ. εἴων
					ἐξιέναι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					18.447
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐξενεγκὼν θ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Ar.
					<u>Ach.</u>
					359
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐξέλκειν τινὰ θ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>Eq.</u>
					365
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θ. ἐξιέναι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>V.</u>
					70
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐκχεῖν θ.</span> empty
				<i>outside</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Id.
				<u>Fr.</u>
				306
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">καρδίαν θ. ἔχειν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					E.
					<u>Fr.</u>
					1063.12
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὰ θ.</span>
			<i>outside</i>, opp. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὰ ἔνδον</span>,
				<i><span class="en">
				Id.
				<u>Or.</u>
				604
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θ. ζῳοτοκεῖν</span> or <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ᾠοτοκεῖν</span>, <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>GA</u>
				718b32
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				719b19
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ῥεῖ διὰ τῶ σώματος ἔξω θ. τὰ
				πνεύματα</span> Ti. 
				Locr.
			<i><span class="en">
				102a
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b> c. gen.,
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θ. τῶν νόμων</span>
			<i>without</i> the law, <i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>Ba.</u>
				331
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θ. Ἀττικῶς, ἔξω
			Ἑλληνικῶς</span> Moer.<i><span class="en">
				p.185
			</span></i> P.</div>
